STARTFONT 2.1
COMMENT FONT.WORLD's own glyphs, beside Fusion Pixel 8 px's: the Greek and
COMMENT Cyrillic letters (Fusion's 8 px has none) and the accents every
COMMENT accented letter is composed from (Fusion's own accented capitals drop
COMMENT theirs). gen_textfont.py reads it.
COMMENT
COMMENT The line is 12 rows, 9 above the baseline: capitals stand on the
COMMENT baseline 6 rows high, lower case 4, descenders reach 2 below. A
COMMENT letter's advance is its width and one more.
COMMENT
COMMENT The accents are the combining characters, advance 0; gen_textfont.py
COMMENT centres each over or under the letter it composes, so only its shape
COMMENT counts. Those below are drawn from the baseline down.
FONT -PodBox-World-Medium-R-Normal--12-120-75-75-P-40-ISO10646-1
SIZE 12 75 75
FONTBOUNDINGBOX 8 12 0 -3
STARTPROPERTIES 3
FONT_ASCENT 9
FONT_DESCENT 3
FAMILY_NAME "PodBox World"
ENDPROPERTIES
